The L1, gate and replay scripts of round.md §3.4 in .refactor/tools/ (planning files only, not in
the PR's final diff): l1.sh (full jest --ci --json with each red test rerun once alone, next
typegen, tsc, eslint -f json, then gates.sh, all under the L1 locks), gates.sh, gate-1 to gate-12
with 1b and 4b over a shared gate-lib.mjs, base.sh and base-tsv.mjs (X/base/ from 24f808b's git
objects and WS0's jest run), rerun.mjs and replay.sh (L3). Paths are followed through moves.tsv
(M's format), git's -M50% renames from 24f808b and the checkout's own moves.d splits.

Gate 6's baseline (framework-exports.txt: 57 framework files and the two 'use server' modules) and
gate 4b's 104 base cases (gate4b.allow, each with its reason) are taken from 24f808b. gate1.allow,
gate1b.allow, shims.allow and counts.conf hold their formats only: at the base nothing differs.

Dry run on a clean checkout of the branch (src = 24f808b's): jest 290 suites and 8,607 tests
green, tsc 0 errors, eslint 0 errors and 999 warnings, gates 1-12 ok (8 n/a before the node kit),
6.5 minutes under the locks. Each gate was also seen to fail on a planted fault (an expect, a
helper value, a docblock, a stale mock, a mock that leaves a name out, a copied constant, a new
route export, a shim, a lost 'use client', a cycle, a red or missing test, a test added to a base
file, a lint error, a changed golden), and to pass a whole-file move and a split by describe block.

